 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT in relation to authorizing the Thiells-Roseville Fire District to file\nan application for exemption from school taxes and real property taxes",
    "basePrintNo": "S6428",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6428-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Taxation",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6428\n\nSPONSOR: WEBER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act in relation to authorizing the Thiells-Roseville Fire District to\nfile an application for exemption from school taxes and real property\ntaxes\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill would authorize the Thiells-Roseville Fire district to file an\napplication for exemption from school taxes and real property taxes.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of the bill authorizes the town of Haverstraw to accept an\napplication of exemption from school and real property taxes from the\nThiells-Roseville Fire District and specifies the parcels.\n\nSection 2 relates to the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Thiells-Roseville Fire Districtpurchased several parcels in July\n2024. Because of the timing of the purchase, the district was unable to\nbe added as exempt from school and real property taxes. This bill would\nallow the district to apply for exemption.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
